## 9. Lessons Learned

This project demonstrated that a security policy template should not simply
be copied and renamed for another organization.

Policy development requires understanding the organization's business
environment, information assets, users, risks, and security requirements.

I also learned that having technical permission to access a system does not
automatically mean that every use of that access is authorized. Access to
sensitive information should have a legitimate business purpose.

The project also demonstrated the importance of writing policies that are
clear enough for users to understand while still providing requirements
that can be governed, monitored, and enforced.

